Z||000000||Hank is Here||02-12-2001||06:14 PM||||Well  as I think about this more and more I want a sunroof.  Thanks to 007Doug I have most of the parts for one.  Now for those of you who do painting professionally, what do you think it would cost to paint a roof matching the color of the car, pannel already sanded, and also off of the car?  If I do this I want to get a descent paint job on it not a Maaco job.  Do you think it would cost more than $150 or so?  <BR>Also somewhere I saw headliners that were made of fiberglass on the net (hopefully it was not Mr. Mikes)   Anyone know who makes these?||||reg||1
Z||000001||Old Lar||02-12-2001||08:00 PM||||I had the Pontiac dealer remove the front facsia, repaint it(stone chips) and replace it for $136.  I would imagine that you could get the roof repainted for $150 or so.  I have seen some real nice Maaco paint jobs.  They are independent franchises, so quality can vary.<P>The Fiero store sells the solid fiberglass headliner backer board. $99 + shipping.  I just got one for my sun roofed Fiero.  Not yet installed.  They are made by a company in Florida for the Fiero store.  He shows up at the Daytona show, but how do you carry it home?  Frank Martin gave me the name of the company, but I don't find it in my notes.  Frank's e mail is dragon@yourlink.net  if you want to try the manufacturer.||||reg||3
Z||000002||rogergarrison||02-12-2001||11:55 PM||||Id paint one off the car for $150 in urathane in my shop. so sure you can find one around you.||||reg||1
